WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.850
1963.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:06.480
The Bishop of Woolwich, John
Robinson, calls for a new morality.

3
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:10.180
Christians, he writes, should
be guided by love alone,

4
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.020
not by a code handed down from above.

5
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:18.650
3 years later, the American priest Joseph
Fletcher turns the idea into a method.

6
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:23.950
But if love is the only rule, does a
Christian still need any other moral rules?

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.600
In this mission, you'll explore
the kind of love Fletcher meant:

8
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.470
agape, a love that is chosen.

9
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.320
Then you'll read what Jesus and
Paul taught about love and the law,

10
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.630
and see why Fletcher claimed them.

11
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.480
Your mission: find out what part other
rules play when love is in charge.
